@page "/docs/get-started/create-app"
@inject ApiMetadata Api

@* A new app from the izzy-blazor starter (catalog/izzy-blazor, published as IzzyBlazor.Templates). The
   options are the starter's, as izzy describe izzy-blazor lists them. *@

<ArticlePage Section="get-started" Slug="create-app">
    <Lead>
        IzzyBlazor's starter is Microsoft's Blazor Web App rebuilt with IzzyBlazor: its layout, pages and account pages
        drawn with IzzyBlazor's components and theme, in every render mode. It takes the same options as
        <Code>dotnet new blazor</Code>.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <Heading Level="2">Install the templates</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            The starter is a <Code>dotnet new</Code> template, like Microsoft's own <Code>blazor</Code> template. Microsoft's
            come with the .NET SDK; IzzyBlazor's come in a NuGet package, so add them to <Code>dotnet new</Code> once, with
            the .NET 10 SDK:
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="bash">@Install</Code>
        <TextBlock>
            The version is there because IzzyBlazor is in preview: without one, <Code>dotnet new install</Code> looks for a
            stable release.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Create the app</Heading>
        <Code Block Language="bash">@Create</Code>
        <TextBlock>
            Open the address <Code>dotnet run</Code> prints. The app has a sidebar, a home page, and sample Counter, Weather
            and Contact pages. Its pages are <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">static</Anchor> by default, and a page
            runs on the server over a circuit once you give it a render mode. Counter has one.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Choose the render modes</Heading>
        <TextBlock>The render mode options are Microsoft's, with the same names and defaults:</TextBlock>
        <Table Items="RenderModes" Caption="Render mode options" Size="ControlSize.Sm" Class="site-params" Bordered="false">
            <Columns>
                <TemplateColumn Title="Option" Width="Length.Rem(17)"><code>@context!.Option</code></TemplateColumn>
                <TemplateColumn Title="What you get">@context!.Result</TemplateColumn>
            </Columns>
        </Table>
        <TextBlock>
            With WebAssembly or Auto, the app is two projects: <Code>MyApp</Code> on the server and <Code>MyApp.Client</Code>
            for the components that run in the browser. See
            <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes#pages-in-the-browser">Pages in the browser</Anchor>.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Accounts</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            <Code>--auth Individual</Code> adds sign-in, registration and account management with ASP.NET Core Identity,
            with accounts in a SQLite database (<Code>--use-local-db</Code> for SQL Server LocalDB). The account pages keep
            Microsoft's code and are drawn with IzzyBlazor, so Microsoft's fixes still apply to them.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Theme and layout</Heading>
        <TextBlock>IzzyBlazor's own options set the theme and the shell around every page:</TextBlock>
        <Table Items="Looks" Caption="Theme and layout options" Size="ControlSize.Sm" Class="site-params" Bordered="false">
            <Columns>
                <TemplateColumn Title="Option" Width="Length.Rem(17)"><code>@context!.Option</code></TemplateColumn>
                <TemplateColumn Title="What it does">@context!.Result</TemplateColumn>
            </Columns>
        </Table>
        <TextBlock>For a dense admin app with links across the top:</TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="bash">dotnet new izzy-blazor -n Admin --preset Compact --brand teal --nav Top</Code>
        <TextBlock>
            Run <Code>dotnet new izzy-blazor --help</Code> for the rest, such as <Code>--no-https</Code> and
            <Code>--use-program-main</Code>. You can change the theme later in <Code>IzzyTheme</Code>; see
            <Anchor Href="docs/theming/themes">Themes and presets</Anchor>.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">With the izzy CLI</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            <Code>izzy new</Code> makes the same app, with the same options. Install the CLI to add
            <Anchor Href="blocks">blocks</Anchor> to the app afterwards; see <Anchor Href="docs/cli/overview">The izzy CLI</Anchor>.
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="bash">izzy new izzy-blazor -n MyApp</Code>

        <Heading Level="2">Next steps</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/cli/overview">The izzy CLI</Anchor>: add a hero, pricing or a sign-up form to the app as code you own.</ListItem>
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/components">Components</Anchor>: every component, with what it does in each render mode.</ListItem>
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/get-started/ai-assistants">AI assistants</Anchor>: <Code>--mcp</Code> connects yours to IzzyBlazor's docs.</ListItem>
        </List>
    </ChildContent>
</ArticlePage>

@code {
    private sealed record Choice(string Option, string Result);

    private string Install => $"dotnet new install IzzyBlazor.Templates@{Api.Version}";

    private const string Create = """
        dotnet new izzy-blazor -n MyApp
        cd MyApp
        dotnet run
        """;

    private static readonly Choice[] RenderModes =
    [
        new("--interactivity Server", "The default. Pages are static, and a page you mark runs on the server over a circuit."),
        new("--interactivity None", "Every page static. The app never opens a circuit."),
        new("--interactivity WebAssembly", "A page you mark runs in the browser, from a .Client project."),
        new("--interactivity Auto", "A page you mark runs on the server at first, and in the browser once WebAssembly has loaded."),
        new("--all-interactive", "Every page interactive in the chosen mode, except pages marked to stay static, such as the account pages."),
    ];

    private static readonly Choice[] Looks =
    [
        new("--preset <name>", "The theme: Standard, or Compact for data and admin apps, Soft for consumer apps, Editorial for reading and docs."),
        new("--brand <color>", "The brand color: blue, ink, indigo, violet, teal, green or rose, or a hex color such as #0a7d5a."),
        new("--nav Top", "Navigation across the top bar, folding into a menu on phones, in place of the sidebar."),
        new("--shell <look>", "How the shell sets the page apart: Tinted (the default), Inset (a raised panel), Flat (lines alone) or Canvas (a tinted page for cards)."),
        new("--content-width <rem>", "How wide pages get: Full, or 64, 72 or 80 rem. Auto, the default, fills the space beside a sidebar and centers 72 under a top bar."),
        new("--empty", "Leaves out the sample pages and the sidebar."),
        new("--mcp", "Connects Claude Code, VS Code, Visual Studio and Cursor to IzzyBlazor's docs server."),
    ];
}
